;; S-12 (catalog §4) — RUN 8: two-agent finding consultation, THE demo
;; bar (PRD §1). Agent A researches + stores findings; fresh agent B is
;; asked a RELATED question on the SAME store — no fixtures, A's output
;; IS B's fixture (the accumulation thesis). The pass bar: B's FIRST
;; eval consults the stored my.kb.* knowledge rows before any repo
;; search.
;; Run 7's agent #2 answered RIGHT while behaving WRONG (re-derived a
;; stored answer in a flawless 70s pipeline) — consults-findings is
;; therefore graded mechanically, SEPARATE from the judged answer
;; correctness.
;;
;; DEEPSEEK TIER — costs real money. The driver refuses to run it
;; unless called with {:seon.gym/allow-paid? true} + DEEPSEEK_API_KEY.
{:seon.gym.scenario/id     :s12-run8-two-agent-consultation
 :seon.gym.scenario/doc    "RUN 8: agent A researches transact-time schema validation and stores my.kb knowledge rows; fresh agent B (same store) must CONSULT those rows FIRST for a related question, then reply."
 :seon.gym.scenario/tier   :paid
 :seon.gym.scenario/status :active
 :seon.gym.scenario/competency :db-memory
 :seon.gym.scenario/axes   [:sees-question :searches-first :consults-findings
                            :stores-proactively :replies-honestly :terminates]
 :seon.gym.scenario/turns
 [{:seon.gym.turn/agent   :a
   :seon.gym.turn/message "How does seon validate schemas at transact time? Walk me through what actually happens when I transact an attribute that was never registered. Store what you find so the next agent doesn't have to redo this."}
  {:seon.gym.turn/agent   :b
   :seon.gym.turn/message "Where exactly does seon check the VALUES of an entity against their Malli schemas during a transact, and what error do I get back when a value doesn't conform?"}]
 :seon.gym.scenario/predicates
 [{:seon.gym.predicate/id     :a-stored-at-least-two-findings-with-provenance
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :stores-proactively
   ;; WIDENED per fix-everything PRD §2 (DECIDED, user 2026-06-11):
   ;; provenance-SHAPED storage in ANY namespace counts — the predicate
   ;; measures the BEHAVIOR (a durable finding row carrying
   ;; source-path/source-line/confidence-shaped provenance), not the
   ;; VOCABULARY (:my.kb/* vs a self-minted :my.kb.<domain>/* sibling).
   ;; Anchored on attr NAMES via the engine's `name` built-in; the
   ;; core registers no other attrs with these names (verified
   ;; 2026-06-11 — only :my.kb/* carries them), so no vacuous pass.
   ;; (2026-06-11 evening: the consult anchor below WIDENED too — any
   ;; store read counts; the judge carries answer quality. The earlier
   ;; "stay strict on :my.kb[./]" stance is superseded by that
   ;; decision.)
   ;; SHAPE NOTE (engine pin, verified live 2026-06-11): TWO datom
   ;; patterns with DISTINCT unbound attr vars joined on one entity
   ;; throw \"Cannot compare <keyword> to\" in datahike-cljs — so the
   ;; remaining name checks ride a nested `q` (one unbound-attr
   ;; pattern per query level) + set/contains?, all engine built-ins.
   ;; Falsified both ways: matches :my.kb/* AND forked :my.kb.<domain>/*
   ;; rows; excludes a source-path+source-line row missing confidence.
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?f
                               :where
                               [?f ?pa _] [(name ?pa) ?pn] [(= ?pn "source-path")]
                               [(q [:find [?n ...] :in $ ?e :where [?e ?a _] [(name ?a) ?n]] $ ?f) ?names]
                               [(set ?names) ?nameset]
                               [(contains? ?nameset "source-line")]
                               [(contains? ?nameset "confidence")]]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect [:count>= 2]}
  ;; Toolbelt renamed seon.search/seon.fs → seon.agent.search/seon.agent.fs
  ;; in 06de140 (batch-2 reorg) — the pattern tracks the CURRENT names.
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id      :a-searched-the-repo
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind    :eval-count-matching
   :seon.gym.predicate/agent   :a
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis    :searches-first
   :seon.gym.predicate/pattern "seon\\.agent\\.search/grep|seon\\.agent\\.fs/read-file"
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect  [:count>= 1]}
  ;; THE pass bar (PRD §1): B's earliest message-driven eval READS THE
  ;; STORE. WIDENED anchor (DECIDED, user 2026-06-11 — same behavior-
  ;; not-vocabulary logic as the §2 provenance widening): "consulted
  ;; first" = the first eval's SOURCE contains a seon.db READ op
  ;; (query/pull/entity/store-inventory) — ANY store read counts, not
  ;; just :my.kb-anchored ones. The previous ":my\\.kb[./]" anchor
  ;; punished a vocabulary choice: a B that queried A's findings under
  ;; a forked spelling HAD consulted; the judge below still measures
  ;; whether the consult paid off in the answer. V4 consult evidence:
  ;; B's creation turn runs `(seon.db/store-inventory)` for real, so
  ;; A's stored kinds sit in B's own transcript (the catalogs are GONE
  ;; — context-v4 V4-3); creation-turn tutorial evals are excluded
  ;; from 'first eval' by the driver's woken-by scoping, so this
  ;; measures B's first MESSAGE-DRIVEN move. (Falsified both ways in
  ;; driver_test's consult-anchor tests.)
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id      :b-first-eval-consults-stored-findings
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind    :first-eval-matches
   :seon.gym.predicate/agent   :b
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis    :consults-findings
   :seon.gym.predicate/pattern "seon\\.db/(query|pull|entity|store-inventory)"}
  ;; "B sent a message onward" — from B with hops>0 (replies to the
  ;; user carry waking-hops+1; the turn-log self-folds carry 0). NOT
  ;; the user-entity join: the datahike-cljs engine mis-binds queries
  ;; joining two identity attrs through one message (pinned repro in
  ;; driver_test's two-agent scenario).
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :b-replied-to-the-user
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :replies-honestly
   :seon.gym.predicate/args   [:seon.gym.agent/b]
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?m
                               :in $ ?bid
                               :where
                               [?ag :seon.agent/id ?bid]
                               [?m :seon.agent.message/from ?ag]
                               [?m :seon.agent.message/hops ?h]
                               [(pos? ?h)]]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect :non-empty}
  ;; G5 — multi-segment finding namespace, no :finding/* fork.
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :no-single-segment-finding-fork
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :stores-proactively
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?f :where [?f :finding/claim ?c]]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect :empty}
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :both-agents-end-idle
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :terminates
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?a
                               :where
                               [?a :seon.agent/id _]
                              (not [?a :seon.agent/terminated-at _])
                              (not-join [?a]
                                [?r :seon.agent.run/agent ?a]
                                [?r :seon.agent.run/status :open])]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect [:count 2]}
  ;; P21 #35 deferred predicates (gym-upgrade §8): each agent's loop
  ;; terminates UNDER the turns-cap (seon.ctx/default-turns-cap = 20)
  ;; by its own stop policy — same shape as S-01/S-21. Per-agent
  ;; turn counts via the designator args; <= 19 incl. the creation
  ;; turn means the cap never fired.
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :a-terminates-under-cap
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :terminates
   :seon.gym.predicate/args   [:seon.gym.agent/a]
   ;; run model: turns are counted agent ← run ← turn (the old
   ;; :seon.agent/sessions / :seon.agent.session/turns model is gone — a
   ;; query on those unregistered attrs returns [] and passes <= 19
   ;; VACUOUSLY, hiding a cap-overrun). Mirrors seon.derive/agent-turn-count.
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?t
                               :in $ ?aid
                               :where
                               [?ag :seon.agent/id ?aid]
                               [?r :seon.agent.run/agent ?ag]
                               [?t :seon.agent.turn/run ?r]]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect [:count<= 19]}
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id     :b-terminates-under-cap
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind   :datalog
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis   :terminates
   :seon.gym.predicate/args   [:seon.gym.agent/b]
   :seon.gym.predicate/query  [:find ?t
                               :in $ ?bid
                               :where
                               [?ag :seon.agent/id ?bid]
                               [?r :seon.agent.run/agent ?ag]
                               [?t :seon.agent.turn/run ?r]]
   :seon.gym.predicate/expect [:count<= 19]}
  ;; --- judged answer correctness, SEPARATE from the behavior bits ---
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id        :judge-a-answer-two-step-gate
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind      :llm-judge
   :seon.gym.predicate/agent     :a
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis      :replies-honestly
   ;; Ground truth updated for the V3-A db split (af417a0): validators
   ;; moved to src/seon/db/internal.cljs; the public face seon.db/transact!
   ;; (src/seon/db.cljs) awaits transact!* and catches EVERY rejection —
   ;; errors are values at the surface. The errors-are-values bar is
   ;; unchanged and strict.
   :seon.gym.predicate/rubric    "PASS only if the reply correctly describes seon's TWO-STEP transact gate — (1) attribute-registration check (an attr never registered via seon.schema/register! is rejected before the tx reaches the database), then (2) per-value Malli validation of entity values — AND grounds it with a real file citation (src/seon/db.cljs or src/seon/db/internal.cljs — the validators live in internal.cljs, the public transact! face in db.cljs). The reply must state that the failure comes back to the caller as an error VALUE ({:seon.db/ok? false :seon.db/error ...}), not a thrown exception. Vague hand-waving about 'validation happens' without the registration-check/value-check distinction fails. NOTE: a reply that describes the INTERNAL validators throwing while seon.db/transact! catches and converts the throw into the envelope is CORRECT (that is the ground truth); only a claim that the CALLER sees a throw/rejection fails."
   :seon.gym.predicate/reference "Ground truth (SHAPE-level, no line pins): validate-attrs! in src/seon/db/internal.cljs rejects any tx whose attr is not registered in seon.schema before the tx reaches datahike; validate-entity-values! in src/seon/db/internal.cljs Malli-validates every entity value against the registered attr schema. Both throw INTERNALLY, but the public face seon.db/transact! (src/seon/db.cljs) awaits transact!* and catches every rejection — the caller NEVER sees a throw: it resolves to {:seon.db/ok? false :seon.db/error ...} on failure and {:seon.db/ok? true ...} on success."}
  {:seon.gym.predicate/id        :judge-b-answer-value-validation
   :seon.gym.predicate/kind      :llm-judge
   :seon.gym.predicate/agent     :b
   :seon.gym.predicate/axis      :replies-honestly
   ;; Ground truth updated for the V3-A db split (af417a0) — see judge-a.
   ;; JUDGE CALIBRATION (post-Wave-A sweep 1, 2026-06-11): the judge
   ;; failed a ground-truth-conformant reply that correctly traced
   ;; "internal throw -> transact! catch -> envelope" by misreading the
   ;; internal-throw description as a caller-facing throw claim. The
   ;; rubric now states the internal/surface distinction explicitly —
   ;; this calibrates the judge to the reference facts it already had;
   ;; agents never see rubrics.
   :seon.gym.predicate/rubric    "PASS only if the reply names validate-entity-values! (or unambiguously locates the per-value Malli validation step) in src/seon/db/internal.cljs and describes the error envelope shape — {:seon.db/ok? false :seon.db/error ...} returned to the caller as a VALUE when a value doesn't conform. IMPORTANT: a reply that says the INTERNAL validator throws an ex-info which seon.db/transact! catches and converts into the envelope is CORRECT — that is exactly the ground truth; do NOT fail it for describing the internal throw. FAIL only if the reply claims the CALLER of seon.db/transact! receives a thrown exception / rejected promise as the surface behavior, or cites a file other than src/seon/db/internal.cljs (or src/seon/db.cljs) for the value check."
   :seon.gym.predicate/reference "Ground truth (SHAPE-level, no line pins): validate-entity-values! in src/seon/db/internal.cljs Malli-validates every entity value against the registered attr schema during transact. It throws INTERNALLY, but the public face seon.db/transact! (src/seon/db.cljs) awaits transact!* and catches every rejection — a non-conforming value resolves to {:seon.db/ok? false :seon.db/error ...} (errors are values at the surface — the caller's promise resolves, it does not reject/throw)."}]}
